text.section:
No insurer or rate service organization shall:

Combine or conspire with any other person to monopolize or attempt to monopolize the business of insurance or any kind, subdivision or class of insurance;


Agree with any other insurer or rate service organization to charge or adhere to any rate, although insurers and rate service organizations may continue to exchange statistical information;


Make any agreement with any other insurer, rate service organization or other person to restrain trade unreasonably;


Make any agreement with any other insurer, rate service organization or other person that may substantially lessen competition in any kind, subdivision or class of insurance; or


Make any agreement with any other insurer or rate service organization to refuse to deal with any person in connection with the sale of insurance.
